<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><em id="A3.F9.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Stable Diffusion 3</em></figcaption>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span><span id="A3.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qualitative results for unconditional generation across backbones.</span> For each model (SD1.5/2.1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, SDXL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Podell et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, SD3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Esser et al., 2024</a>)</cite>), the top row shows baseline sampling and the bottom row shows +TAG at matched NFEs. TAG yields sharper, more coherent structure with fewer artifacts while preserving diversity.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
